WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.900
Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday. Current me is actually on vacation, so this video is being made by five days ago me/ I hope it has been a calm, and peaceful five days.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:13.080
Anyway it's Question Tuesday, the day that I answer real questions from real Nerdfighters, let's get right to it!

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:14.600
Q: Can we start with some good news?

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:21.580
A: Yeah there's a pretty good chance that no humans will contract polio this week,  which is something we've very rarely been able to say over the last several thousand years.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:25.400
Advanced trials of an Ebola vaccine showed a 100% effectiveness rate

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:29.080
The U.S. economy has added jobs for 76 consecutive months

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:30.140
Plus Beyonce is pregnant

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:31.820
a new Zelda game is forthcoming

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:40.380
And humans, on average, are living longer, healthier and more prosperous lives than they were yesterday, or the day before that, or at any time in human history

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:43.040
Q: Diet Dr. Pepper or Cherry Diet Dr. Pepper?

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:44.840
While we're on the topic of good news

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:47.480
it is almost impossible to find Cherry Diet Dr. Pepper these days

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:51.980
which is great news, because Diet Dr. Pepper on its own is already perfect

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:53.820
Q:What's your opinion on bears?

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.320
Um, strongly in favor

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:56.140
In favor

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:56.820
Meh

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:57.720
In favor

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:59.200
Honestly, a little overrated

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:00.320
Opposed to

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:01.120
And in favor

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:02.300
Q: What's your opinion of glitter?

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:04.300
Sometimes Alice will put glitter on my face

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:07.100
And then like several days later even after many face washes

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.320
I'll discover there's still like one or two little pieces of glitter

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:14.700
And then I think 'you know, if glitter can do that billions of bacteria probably can too

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:18.420
Q: If you had a Tardis and could go anywhere in space and time, where would you go?

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:24.540
Well the past was worse, and I'm not feeling like totally confident in the future, so I would probably just go to present day New Zealand

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:26.360
because those people seem nice

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:28.360
Q: Why hasn't live news taken off on YouTube?

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:31.880
Let me answer your question with a question. Do we really need more live news?

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:37.960
What I need is like a pause button that, like, contextualizes the news for me and tells me what it means

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:40.680
Q: How are you coping with all the scary stuff in the world?

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:44.060
I don't know what you're talking about, I am a happy lobster in a pot of cool water

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:46.120
Does anyone else feel like the water is getting warmer?

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:48.300
Q: How excited are you for VidCon Europe in April?

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:51.180
Very excited. Not least because I haven't been back to Amsterdam

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:54.740
since The Fault in Our Stars move came out, and it will be fun to go to all of my old haunts.

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:56.740
Q: Any YA book recommendations?

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:59.920
Yes. The Hate U Give by Angie Thomas, which comes out later this month

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:01.920
And I truly believe it will be a classic.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:05.600
Like, even if you don't love books you are going to love this book

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:09.900
I try not to inundate you with book recommendations but this is a very special book

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:11.900
Q: What's been your favorite part of 100 Days so far?

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:14.780
I think my favorite thing is how bad Chris and I are at high fives

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:19.820
Like we've been best friends for a decade without ever successfully completing a single high five

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:21.180
Q: Favorite song on the Hamilton mixtape?

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:21.880
Immigrants

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:23.140
Q: What's the secret of life?

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:26.020
I think maybe understanding that you deserve to love and be loved

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:28.020
Q: All-time favorite dystopia novel?

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:30.880
Yeah, I don't know. 1984 is definitely a great dystopia novel

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:34.180
but I feel like the one that we're living in has just amazing world building

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:35.580
Q: What's your favorite Pokemon?

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:39.460
Henry says the answer to this question is 'mega mewtwo ex'. Whatever that means

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:42.620
Q: What’s the most important song you’ve ever listened to?

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:47.720
John: That’s a great question because, of course, the most important songs you’ve ever listened are not necessarily the best ones.

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:52.600
There’ve been a few occasions in my life when a song crossed my path that I actually like needed

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:58.240
that gave form or expression to something deep down inside me that I couldn’t understand or look directly at.

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:02.760
The first one was probably the song I Think We're Alone Now by 1980's teen idol Tiffany

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:06.640
But also New Partner by the Palace Brothers, Love Love Love by the Mountain Goats

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:10.620
I put together a playlist of songs this question brought to my mind it's in the doobly doo below

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:15.280
Nerdfighters, I'd love to hear what songs or art in general you feel like are important to to you

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:17.740
And maybe we can discover cool stuff from each other

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:19.220
Alright, Hank. It's time for me to vacate.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:21.440
I will see you on Friday.

